35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Shizue, the complaint log shows one house filed most complaints. @Rin, the frontages vary wildly. How do we share fairly without blaming anyone?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, that is a heavy burden for one family. I hope the station block’s minutes help us avoid similar arguments about small chores.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, the truck arrives before most wake. Filing requires four months and five signatures. This is a significant, recurring time cost.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, the frontages are totally different! One house is tiny. @Asuka, four months is forever! We can’t just let one family carry this forever.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, four months is a long wait. @Rin, the ledger shows thirty-four thousand yen yearly in waste. We must balance time and money.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, I hear you. But @Servas, thirty-four thousand yen is a lot. How do we split that fairly without starting another fight?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I worry about the daily reality. The station block argued over sweeping. We must choose a plan that keeps our mornings peaceful, not just fair on paper.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, peace is not a metric. I need to know the exact recurring hours for maintenance. Can we calculate the weekly time cost per household?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, math is cool, but people matter more! @Kenji, if one house is tiny, they can’t carry the big bin. We need a rotating schedule!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, rotation is wise. @Kenji, the subsidy covers forty percent, capped at ninety thousand. We must calculate the true share before dividing.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, rotation sounds good! @Servas, if the subsidy helps, maybe we split the rest by frontage? I just want us to still talk after this.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, a rotating schedule sounds kind. I hope it prevents the small daily arguments the station block had. Let us keep our mornings gentle.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, rotation is a variable, not a solution. I need the specific weekly hours for setup and maintenance to calculate the true burden.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I know you like numbers, but the meeting showed nobody wants to be the ""police""! We need a plan where everyone shares the work, not just the money!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, time is precious, but money is the root. With the subsidy, our true cost drops. Let us agree on a fair split before calculating hours.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Everyone, I’m glad we’re finding common ground. Let’s pick a plan that keeps our doors open, not just our ledgers balanced. Ready for options?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I am ready. I hope the options show us a way to keep our mornings quiet and our neighbours smiling.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am ready. I will evaluate the options strictly by their recurring time cost. We must not ignore the operational burden.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I’m ready! I just need to make sure the tiny house isn’t stuck with the bin forever. Let’s see the options!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,I am ready. Let us see which path balances our wallets and our friendships.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
